{
  "id": "coding_agents_tamp",
  "title": "Coding Agents for Generalized TAMP",
  "category": "model_showdown",
  "hook_tag": "MODEL SHOWDOWN: TAMP AUTOMATION",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "How do we bridge the gap between abstract task logic and physical robot motion? Can coding agents solve TAMP without exhaustive, hand-engineered geometric planning?",
      "visual_focus": "A split screen showing a complex robot planning tree on the left and a clean Python script on the right.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "Coding Agents": "#38BDF8",
        "TAMP": "#F59E0B"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "Traditional TAMP solvers face a catastrophic combinatorial explosion, where discrete task decisions are tightly coupled to continuous geometric constraints, making scaling near impossible for new environments.",
      "visual_focus": "A collapsing grid graph representing the exponential branching factor of traditional planners.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "combinatorial explosion": "#EF4444",
        "tightly coupled": "#EF4444"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "Instead of manual heuristics, we treat planning as a synthesis task; agents interact with simulators to develop programs that generalize across unseen instances and object counts.",
      "visual_focus": "An agent's feedback loop connecting a simulation environment to a code synthesis engine.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "synthesis task": "#34D399",
        "generalize": "#34D399"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "The mechanism relies on calibrating physical models through iterative interaction, testing edge cases, and freezing logic into robust programs before evaluating on Held-out test instances.",
      "visual_focus": "A block diagram showing the Program Synthesis, Interaction, and Frozen Evaluation loop.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "iterative interaction": "#F59E0B",
        "Frozen": "#F59E0B"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "Agents outperform classical planners, achieving a 95% success rate while requiring ten times less computation per instance across ninety-eight thousand simulated episodes of robot motion.",
      "visual_focus": "A bar chart comparing agent success (95%) versus baseline planner success (47%).",
      "highlight_words": {
        "95%": "#34D399",
        "ten times less": "#34D399"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 6,
      "text": "Follow The Model Verse for the engineering behind modern AI architectures and the future of autonomous planning agents.",
      "visual_focus": "The Model Verse logo appearing on a clean chalkboard background.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "The Model Verse": "#34D399"
      }
    }
  ],
